column1:
Jody Steadman reported that attempts to access Stargate via Apache Knox using curl ends with 413 error when the following conditions are met:  AD is being used directly for Kerberos The knox principal is configured to require Kerberos pre-auth Stargate is using SPNEGO Pre-auth errors exist in Kerberos debug log output  [~sumit.gupta] found that the gateway logs in the environment provided by Jody Steadman has the following error: {code} 2015-04-20 14:24:21 660 DEBUG http.headers (DefaultClientConnection.java:sendRequestHeader(273)) - >> GET /version?doAs=jsteadman HTTP/1.1 2015-04-20 14:24:21 661 DEBUG http.headers (DefaultClientConnection.java:sendRequestHeader(276)) - >> Host: node1.jodylaptop.net:60080 2015-04-20 14:24:21 661 DEBUG http.headers (DefaultClientConnection.java:sendRequestHeader(276)) - >> Connection: Keep-Alive 2015-04-20 14:24:21 661 DEBUG http.headers (DefaultClientConnection.java:sendRequestHeader(276)) - >> User-Agent: Apache-HttpClient/4.2.5 (java 1.5) 2015-04-20 14:24:21 661 DEBUG http.headers (DefaultClientConnection.java:sendRequestHeader(276)) - >> Authorization: Negotiate  2015-04-20 14:24:21 664 DEBUG http.wire (Wire.java:wire(63)) - << ""HTTP/1.1 413 FULL head[][
]"" 2015-04-20 14:24:21 665 DEBUG http.wire (Wire.java:wire(63)) - << ""Connection: close[][
]"" 2015-04-20 14:24:21 666 DEBUG http.wire (Wire.java:wire(63)) - << ""[][
]"" {code} Sumit suggested using large buffer size in hbase REST Server to get rid of the ""FULL Head"" error 413 Error with Stargate through Knox  using AD  SPNEGO  and Pre-Auth
